<title>JAPAN: Marubeni to post 28 bln yen stock appraisal loss.</title>
<headline>Marubeni to post 28 bln yen stock appraisal loss.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading house Marubeni Corp said on Friday that it would post an appraisal loss of about 28 billion yen on its securities holdings in the year to March 31, 1997, due to sluggish stock prices.</p>
<p>The company announced earlier on Friday that it had lowered its parent current profit forecast for 1996/97 to 15 billion yen from its previous forecast of 40 billion yen. Its actua1 1995/96 parent current profit was 39.17 billion yen.</p>
</text>
